{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For therefore I have seen your face.</b> It seems to me the verse means: take, I pray you, my present from me, for therefore — in order that you may accept me — have I seen your face with this present, like one who sees the face of princes and judges, whose custom is to precede them with a gift." "<b>And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted:</b> ״כראות פני אלהים״ — 'as one sees the face of Elohim.' Rabbi Yohanan said: it is permitted to flatter the wicked in this world, for it is said, ״כי על כן ראיתי פניך״. And this disputes the view of Rabbi Pedat, for Rabbi Pedat said (Psalms 101:7): ״דובר שקרים לא יכון לנגד עיני״ — 'he who speaks falsehood shall not be established before my eyes' — and it is written (Job 13:16): ״כי לא לפניו חנף יבא״ — 'for a flatterer shall not come before Him.' The opinion of Rabbi Yohanan is that it is permitted to flatter the wicked on account of fear, for so Jacob flattered Esau; and the opinion of Rabbi Pedat is that even on account of fear it is forbidden, as it is said, ״דובר שקרים״ and so forth. But the flattery that Jacob practiced toward Esau — such flattery is permitted, because it is language that bears two senses, one of praise and one of disgrace: for ראיתי can bear a contemptuous sense, as in (Psalms 22:18): ״יביטו יראו בי״. And likewise אלהים can bear the sense of idolatry. And if the wicked understands it in the sense of praise, there is no concern in this; as our Rabbis interpreted: 'he misleads himself — I do not mislead him.' And so the Sages permitted a Torah scholar to say עבדא דנורא אנא — 'I am a servant of the awesome one' — in order that they let him be regarding the tax, because it is language that bears two senses: a sense of idolatry, such as מולך, or a sense of a servant of HaShem, blessed be He, who is likened to fire, as it is written of Him (Deuteronomy 4:24): ״אש אוכלה הוא״. And language of this kind, which is heard in two senses, is permitted on account of fear even according to Rabbi Pedat."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:27.764500950Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}